# Line endings.
#
# The Lean generators write LF, and `cargo xtask check-golden` asserts
# `git diff --exit-code test_data/` to catch the ground truth drifting away from the
# Lean that produced it. On a Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf` on, that file comes
# back out with CRLF, so regenerating rewrites all 822 lines and the gate reports a
# difference where the bytes actually agree. Pinning these to LF removes the false
# positive; it is the one place where a line ending changes a pass into a fail.
#
# The rest of the tree is left to `core.autocrlf`. Normalising it as well would be
# tidier, but it is a renormalisation commit touching every file, and nothing depends
# on it.
test_data/*.json text eol=lf

# Lean and Python sources are read and written by toolchains that expect LF.
*.lean text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
